// Ch3 B11 "The dock at night" (docs/kb/story/beats/vertical_slice.md): after the Drownbell, Haluna at
// night (H10: lamps in the windows, sea-glow, stars). Rhen finds Asha at the end of the dock and asks
// to come as a guardian. She says yes before Toma, arriving, can object; his objection becomes a sigh
// and "Then you walk behind me." Nobody speaks of what the pilgrimage ends in (that's Ch4). If Rhen
// asked Toma on the steps (ch03_rhen_asked_after), he almost asks her too, and she asks about his day
// first, her tell (voice_guide.md), and he lets her. In-engine; Toma walks up the dock mid-scene.
// M2-FP-115: an E scene (vertical_slice.md: no letterbox, the player keeps the camera rail), so the staging is in
// the bodies: Rhen walks out to her at the dock end, they turn to each other, and she turns to Toma for her answer.
title: ch03_dock_at_night
location: ch02/haluna
---
// M2-FP-119: the player sets the scene off from anywhere on the dock, so the walk is as long as it is:
// the scene waits for him to reach her, then a breath before either turns.
@mark rhen rhen_by_asha walk
@wait arrive=rhen
// M2-FP-119: Toma starts at the dock's root, behind H04's lens (he had stood on its axis, his shield filling the
// opening frame and hiding Rhen), and walks up the whole dock: DockEnd looks back up it, so he comes up in the
// background while they talk and arrives on his own last line, as the beat says. He sets off only once Rhen is
// at Asha's side (well inside DockEnd), because his way passes through H04's lens.
@mark toma dock_toma walk
@wait 0.6
@anim rhen look_at asha
@anim asha look_at rhen
<<if $ch03_rhen_asked_after>>
Rhen [neutral]: Asha. On the shrine steps, Toma said... #line:ch03_dock_001
Asha [soft_smile]: How was your day, Rhen? Truly. #line:ch03_dock_002
Rhen [tender]: ...Long. Good, mostly. #line:ch03_dock_003
<<endif>>
// M4-A2P-115 A1: nobody tells Rhen when she leaves (the market's "Two days..." are overheard pieces he misses the sum
// of), so he asks, from the bag he saw at Neme's, and she tells him.
Rhen [neutral]: You're leaving, aren't you? The bag at Neme's. #line:ch03_dock_012
Asha [neutral]: The day after tomorrow. At first tide. The causeway won't wait for me. #line:ch03_dock_005
Rhen [determined]: Then let me come. As your guardian. I can dive, and I can carry, and I don't scare. #line:ch03_dock_006
Asha [smile]: Yes. #line:ch03_dock_007
Toma [worried]: Asha. A guardian is not chosen on a dock, at night— #line:ch03_dock_008
@anim asha look_at toma
Asha [tender]: This one was, Toma. #line:ch03_dock_009
Toma [exhausted]: ... #line:ch03_dock_010
@wait 0.8
Toma [neutral]: Then you walk behind me. #line:ch03_dock_011
<<set $ch03_rhen_sworn_guardian = true>>
===
